{
  "reviewNotes": [
    "C000560 and CDIR-1999-06-15-OK-H-2 identify Thomas Allen Coburn. CRPT-106hrpt1047 corroborates Commerce and Energy and Power; GAOREPORTS-HEHS-00-54 identifies his Health and Environment vice-chair role. Only the printed Tom A. Coburn cells apply.",
    "F000439 and the same-edition Tennessee biography identify William H.",
    "Frist; contemporary hearings confirm the printed Bill Frist chair roles.",
    "The Directory's Armed Services section prints H.; M000472 and 106th",
    "hearing rosters identify John Michael McHugh of New York instead.",
    "F000328 identifies Tillie Kidd Fowler; her biography confirms both",
    "parent committees and 106th oversight chairmanship. Target cells only.",
    "The Senate's February 23, 2000 statement identifies Robert F. Bennett",
    "as this committee's chair. Only the Directory's Bob Bennett cell applies.",
    "Full printed name is linked to Sam Dale Brownback by B000953/FEC",
    "S6KS00122; 106th Commerce hearing rosters also print Sam Brownback, KS.",
    "The source prints Kent Cochran of ND in two children, while its parent",
    "prints Thad Cochran of MS. The member index and CREC-1999-02-08 D114",
    "confirm Cochran in both: a scoped name/state correction, not an alias.",
    "Same-edition Armed Services parent spells McIntyre correctly; 106th",
    "procurement/readiness hearing rosters independently confirm both seats.",
    "Bioguide D000492 identifies David Timothy Dreier and his 106th Rules",
    "chairmanship; the Directory explicitly prints these three CA cells.",
    "J000032 and contemporary 106th Crime/Immigration hearing rosters",
    "confirm Sheila Jackson Lee, TX. Only these misspelled source cells apply.",
    "Offline-reviewed source cells. These are edition-bound decisions, never",
    "source-provided aliases or a runtime nickname dictionary. Each fingerprint",
    "covers JSON.stringify of the entire parsed roster in its original order."
  ],
